to draw them in the neighborhood of $x=-2$ without taking the pencil off of the paper." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-78132/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "43673f0f-f288-5a25-ae0c-20b9acd75def" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78132/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "c5613c45-5a45-55bb-8746-e2322869f707" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78132/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "baa240db-6d21-5557-b9df-eae150219acc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78132/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "2583eabc-4449-5497-931d-9983ec84f1d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78132/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "dcc3cc9d-6262-5cac-a521-a723606c96de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78132/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "88a91bb7-f7d1-54e0-8fd8-3438bae5b3a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78132/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-78132/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-78132/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-78132/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-78132/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-78132/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78132" :question/id #uuid "2af23e59-69ed-5518-a45b-4d516ea7345c" :question/math-academy-id "q-78132" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831128/assets/890e7eaf519a65ca19d4a90b604e7d7a8ab7054635296c4b08f000546f23b545.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\n- $x=-2$\n- $x=1$\n- $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $-2.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1.$ Since there is a jump at $x=1,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- Therefore, the function $f(x)$ is continuous $x=3.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of  $x=3$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is  \"I and III only\".\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831128/assets/7c96c401ddae0049859fd5608cb08c6ce9ae8a2e6c3db69d7d4b379b3824094e.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-78132/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd6c125-ecaf-5847-a802-ec1b3594a15c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78132"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102115/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "e4586339-52ea-5a00-b9b1-e687d62000a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102115/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "c6ee97ae-fba1-59ff-8520-8be5947cf413" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102115/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "3c8d8d83-d77a-5608-aa19-4cf4da602885" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102115/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "499855ad-f2de-5bd5-aa3a-e1e0312d1100" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102115/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "974e1e94-75aa-51ef-ac38-60c44abfe821" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102115/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd4a4d0a-1b4a-5c41-8cff-1321f5bd08c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102115/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-102115/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-102115/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-102115/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-102115/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-102115/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102115" :question/id #uuid "d542cfea-06a6-5d32-836f-df32a05c8681" :question/math-academy-id "q-102115" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831128/assets/d1d91b2d791d69c512a6bd2e7d523563de076a7f3afda53513234e799152ef8d.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\n- $x=-1$\n- $x=1$\n- $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-1.$ Since there is a jump at $x=-1,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=-1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1.$ Since there is a break at $x=1,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=3.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=3$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is  \"III only\".\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831128/assets/57415045f7a1cc1c896756ff19cb17f90074151a25d12c56068fb6f86a064753.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102115/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd6c125-ecaf-5847-a802-ec1b3594a15c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102115"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48076/selection/1ca69b543c9b28f174a25a7c3f1f3e09a61926580b13cf10535717d7045875f2" :answer/id #uuid "383c71da-c607-5f74-9d61-241a4aab4021" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831128/assets/d4ea3f231a2fced912c584c8fe23a24167e9454ca8e9c8c151020407c62cd51c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48076/selection/9825a331394f8506cdf5b8fac6674edca20261d55e1ad7f3ce06617542a461cf" :answer/id #uuid "dae861b3-326d-5fed-b712-8c1a6084a2e1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831128/assets/8f88e7f270798d0caec08fe3a1929374ca993e1a97d2beb73c51d6f16a5859ee.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48076/selection/33ed80e3739645a5c31d92c1a1d9af5151e9f5399c