academy-id "q-48067" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831128/assets/c132c73b7ca4759882959f9df42110c36e31f3c8af27afa02c0caa20f5f94d52.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. \n\n- $f(x)$ is defined at $x=1$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)=f(1)$\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $f(1)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x) & =1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)=1=f(1).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of $f(x)$ can be drawn without taking our pencil off of the paper in the neighborhood of $x=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48067/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48067"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48062/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "1449ee10-eb98-542c-9545-5d919b90c800" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48062/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "8a246f2e-217f-56a7-b085-efdb384f8745" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48062/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "fdac98e0-36e0-5794-ba57-4e657325937a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48062/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "272ec425-9242-5a79-9ad8-c143c9075d8f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48062/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b1d2ac6f-083c-5660-a925-a9787e203145" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48062/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "793146a7-3cfb-5660-ae6f-4074c81b3907" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48062/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-48062/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-48062/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-48062/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-48062/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-48062/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48062" :question/id #uuid "1e8acf5a-125d-50fa-aa94-a610aec40435" :question/math-academy-id "q-48062" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831128/assets/d9db7f2a491ae3065dbe8434a71d378c4fed8fec16c82e2fd76dcb209c786809.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $f(x)$ is defined at $x=1$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)$ exists\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is false. From the graph we can see that no value has been assigned to $f(x)$ at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x) & =1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)=1.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function is not even defined at $x=1.$ The graph contains a break at $x=1.$ It's impossible to draw the graph of $f(x)$ without taking our pencil off of the paper." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48062/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48062"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48068/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "dd30b332-a8e2-58b7-a9eb-c691cc080975" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48068/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "5db6d7c3-7318-50d6-9300-693b9c2fa834" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48068/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f836507c-6151-54ae-9e4d-daf48edb255b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48068/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "d128c3db-b502-5f30-815c-661d1997e153" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48068/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "afc92a17-14a7-5b6f-8840-3969b42a787c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48068/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d91affc-5743-5eb3-94df-5d6dd7e4d49a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48068/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-fi